# Idris2 proof manifest — read by scripts/check-proofs.sh idris2
# Format: <source-root>|<module-relative-to-source-root>|gated|quarantine|<note>
# gated      = must compile.  quarantine = known-broken, must keep failing.
#
# The Idris2 modules are the interface contract of issue #11 and live with the
# ABI seam in src/interface/Abi/ (module Abi.*), checked from src/interface so
# each module's name matches its path. The harness also scans this root, so a
# new .idr file there is an error until it is listed here.
src/interface|Abi/Tls.idr|gated| the handle lifecycle as linear types (claims LIN-1, LIN-2)
src/interface|Abi/Client.idr|gated| positive control: a complete client typechecks (LIN-3)
src/interface|Abi/Misuse.idr|gated| failing blocks: each misuse must be rejected by the typechecker (LIN-4)
